## select all topics having `searchString` either in `name` , or `description`, or `smartContent.content` field of topic
```
const searchTopics = async (searchString, searchOptions) => {
  const regex = new RegExp(searchString, "i"); // 'i' for case insensitive

  const selectFields = {
    uniqueId: 1,
    name: 1,
    parentId: 1,
    tags: 1,
  };

  const criteria = {
    $or: [
      { name: { $regex: regex } },
      //{ description: { $regex: regex } },
    ],
  };

  if (
    searchOptions &&
    searchOptions.description &&
    searchOptions.description > 0
  ) {
    selectFields.description = 1;
    criteria["$or"].push({ description: { $regex: regex } });
  }

  return await Topic.find(criteria).select(selectFields);
};
```

## update the `parentId` of all children tasks to `taskId`

To update the `parentId` of all children tasks to `taskId`, you can use the `updateMany` method provided by Mongoose. Here's how you can do it:

```javascript
// Route to update a task by ID
router.put("/:id", async (req, res) => {
  const taskId = req.params.id;
  const updatedTask = req.body;

  console.log(`taskId : ${taskId}, updatedTask : ${JSON.stringify(updatedTask)}`);

  try {
    // Get the existing task
    let task = await Task.findById(taskId);

    // Check if the task exists
    if (!task) {
      return res.status(404).json({ message: "Task not found" });
    }

    // Update the parentId of children tasks
    const childrenIds = updatedTask.children || [];
    await Task.updateMany({ _id: { $in: childrenIds } }, { parentId: taskId });

    res.json({ message: "ParentId updated successfully for children tasks" });
  } catch (err) {
    res.status(400).json({ message: err.message });
  }
});
```

In this code:
- We first find the existing task with the given `taskId`.
- Then, we extract the `children` array from the `updatedTask` object.
- We use the `updateMany` method to update the `parentId` of all children tasks whose IDs are present in the `children` array to the `taskId`.


