## Difference Between Factory and Abstract Factory (Java)

Both are **creational design patterns** used for **object creation**, but they differ in **scope and complexity**.

---

## 1. Factory Pattern (Factory Method)

Factory Pattern creates **one type of object based on input**.

Basic idea:

```text id="yupctk"
Factory → Creates single product
```

### Example

```java id="hs2s3n"
interface Vehicle {

    void start();

}
```

Implementations:

```java id="0j1ov3"
class Car implements Vehicle {

    public void start(){
        System.out.println("Car started");
    }

}
```

```java id="ql4n1l"
class Bike implements Vehicle {

    public void start(){
        System.out.println("Bike started");
    }

}
```

Factory class:

```java id="86hl9d"
class VehicleFactory {

    public static Vehicle getVehicle(String type){

        if(type.equals("car"))
            return new Car();

        if(type.equals("bike"))
            return new Bike();

