Here are **industry-level ways** to find the **Maximum Path Sum in a Binary Tree** 👇

---

### 1. Optimized DFS (Most Important 🔥🔥 O(n))

```java id="mps1"
public class MaxPathSum {

    static class Node {
        int val;
        Node left, right;
        Node(int v) { val = v; }
    }

    static int maxSum = Integer.MIN_VALUE;

    static int maxPath(Node root) {
        if (root == null) return 0;

        int left = Math.max(0, maxPath(root.left));
        int right = Math.max(0, maxPath(root.right));

        // path through root
        maxSum = Math.max(maxSum, left + right + root.val);

        // return single path
        return root.val + Math.max(left, right);
    }

    static int maxPathSum(Node root) {
        maxPath(root);
        return maxSum;
    }
}
```

---

### 2. Return Pair (Clean Approach 🔥)

```java id="mps2"
class Pair {
    int maxPath;   // max path anywhere
    int maxDown;   // max downward path

    Pair(int p, int d) {
        maxPath = p;
        maxDown = d;
    }
}

static Pair solve(Node root) {
    if (root == null) return new Pair(Integer.MIN_VALUE, 0);

    Pair left = solve(root.left);
    Pair right = solve(root.right);

    int maxDown = Math.max(root.val,
                    root.val + Math.max(left.maxDown, right.maxDown));

    int throughRoot = root.val + Math.max(0, left.maxDown)
                                 + Math.max(0, right.maxDown);

    int maxPath = Math.max(throughRoot,
                    Math.max(left.maxPath, right.maxPath));

    return new Pair(maxPath, maxDown);
}
```

