## Four Types of Method References

---

## 1. Static Method Reference

```java id="mra1"
class Util {
    static int square(int x) {
        return x * x;
    }
}

Function<Integer, Integer> f = Util::square;
```

---

## 2. Instance Method Reference (of a particular object)

```java id="mra2"
String str = "hello";

Supplier<String> s = str::toUpperCase;

System.out.println(s.get());
```

---

## 3. Instance Method Reference (of an arbitrary object of a class)

```java id="mra3"
List<String> list = Arrays.asList("a", "bb", "ccc");

list.sort(String::compareTo);
```

---

## 4. Constructor Reference

```java id="mra4"
Supplier<List<String>> s = ArrayList::new;

List<String> list = s.get();
```

---

## Quick Summary 🔥

```java id="mra5"
// 1. Class::staticMethod
// 2. obj::instanceMethod
// 3. Class::instanceMethod
// 4. Class::new
```

---

## One-line Answer 💡

👉 The four types of method references are:
**static method, instance method (object), instance method (class), and constructor reference**.

