## `Collectors.groupingBy()` (Java 8)

👉 **Definition (crisp)**
`groupingBy()` is used to **group elements of a stream based on a key** and returns a `Map<K, List<T>>`.

---

## Method (Basic)

```java id="gb1"
Map<K, List<T>> groupingBy(Function<? super T, ? extends K> classifier);
```

---

## Basic Example

```java id="gb2"
List<Integer> list = Arrays.asList(1,2,3,4,5);

Map<Integer, List<Integer>> map = list.stream()
    .collect(Collectors.groupingBy(x -> x % 2));

System.out.println(map);
// {0=[2,4], 1=[1,3,5]}
```

---

## With Strings

```java id="gb3"
List<String> list = Arrays.asList("java", "go", "spring");

Map<Integer, List<String>> map = list.stream()
    .collect(Collectors.groupingBy(s -> s.length()));
```

---

## With Custom Object 🔥

```java id="gb4"
class User {
    String name;
    int age;

    User(String name, int age) {
        this.name = name;
        this.age = age;
    }
}

List<User> users = Arrays.asList(
    new User("Prem", 25),
    new User("Ram", 20),
    new User("Shyam", 25)
);

Map<Integer, List<User>> map = users.stream()
    .collect(Collectors.groupingBy(u -> u.age));
```

---

## Advanced (Downstream Collector)

```java id="gb5"
Map<Integer, Long> count = list.stream()
    .collect(Collectors.groupingBy(
        x -> x % 2,
        Collectors.counting()
    ));
```

---

## Nested Grouping 🔥

```java id="gb6"
Map<Integer, Map<Integer, List<Integer>>> map = list.stream()
    .collect(Collectors.groupingBy(
        x -> x % 2,
        Collectors.groupingBy(x -> x > 2 ? 1 : 0)
    ));
```

---

## Key Points

* Returns `Map<K, List<T>>`
* Groups based on key function
* Supports downstream collectors
* Very useful in real projects

---

## One-line Answer 💡

👉 `Collectors.groupingBy()` is used to **group stream elements into a Map based on a classification function**.

